"{\n \"title\": \"GATE 2027 Syllabus Changes: Sourced Checklist | PadhaiShuru\",\n \"headings\": [\n  \"H1: Syllabus & paper changes\",\n  \"H2: Change checklist\",\n  \"H2: Papers without an itemized change\"\n ],\n \"paragraphs\": [\n  \"Only changes we could trace to an official source are listed. Tick each one off as you update your plan; your ticks stay on this device.\",\n  \"Last verified on 2026-10-02 against the official GATE 2027 brochure (opens in a new tab).\",\n  \"0 of 10 reviewed\",\n  \"The organizing institute states that the syllabus of GATE 2027 test papers has been revised and that the syllabi for most test papers changed. Re-check your paper's official GATE 2027 syllabus before planning revision.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"New test paper. Apart from General Aptitude: Part A (common, 60 marks, 39 questions) plus one of Part B1 Electrical or Part B2 Mechanical (25 marks, 16 questions), chosen during the exam. Part A covers Engineering Mathematics and Basics of Mechatronics.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"TF is no longer a separate paper. Textile Engineering and Fibre Science is now XE9, an optional section of the XE paper (sections: Textile Fibres; Yarn Manufacture; Fabric Manufacture; Textile Testing; Chemical Processing).\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"The common Engineering Mathematics section is now XE0 and the optional sections are numbered XE1 to XE9, with Textile as XE9. Candidates answer XE0 plus at most two of XE1 to XE9. See the brochure's paper table for the full old-to-new mapping.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"XH-B1 (Reasoning and Comprehension, common) is now XH0; XH-C1 to XH-C6 are now XH1 to XH6.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"XL-P (Chemistry, common) is now XL0; XL-Q to XL-U are now XL1 to XL5.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"The GATE 2027 BT syllabus has 6 sections, with bioreaction and bioprocess topics under Section 4, Fundamentals of Biological Engineering. Compare with your previous BT syllabus for topic-level differences.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026), Appendix D (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"The allowed primary/secondary paper combinations include the new RA paper (for example CS, EC, EE, IN and ME can pair with RA). The list is marked tentative and subject to change.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026), Table 4 (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"Applicants must provide live facial details during registration. A verified DigiLocker account is recommended; unverified accounts may be asked for additional documents.\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"GATE 2027 is scheduled for February 6, 7, 13, 14, 20 and 21, 2027 (forenoon and afternoon sessions).\",\n  \"Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"No paper-specific change itemized here as of 2026-10-02. The brochure says most syllabi were revised, so check the official GATE 2027 syllabus on the organizing institute site (https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in).\",\n  \"PadhaiShuru is not affiliated with IIT Madras or GATE. If you spot an error, the official brochure wins. Practise PYQs\"\n ],\n \"listItems\": [\n  \"ALLSyllabusSyllabi of most papers revisedThe organizing institute states that the syllabus of GATE 2027 test papers has been revised and that the syllabi for most test papers changed. Re-check your paper's official GATE 2027 syllabus before planning revision.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"RANew paperNew paper: Robotics and Automation (RA)New test paper. Apart from General Aptitude: Part A (common, 60 marks, 39 questions) plus one of Part B1 Electrical or Part B2 Mechanical (25 marks, 16 questions), chosen during the exam. Part A covers Engineering Mathematics and Basics of Mechatronics.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"TF / XEStructureTextile (TF) becomes XE section XE9TF is no longer a separate paper. Textile Engineering and Fibre Science is now XE9, an optional section of the XE paper (sections: Textile Fibres; Yarn Manufacture; Fabric Manufacture; Textile Testing; Chemical Processing).Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"XEPaper codeXE section codes renamedThe common Engineering Mathematics section is now XE0 and the optional sections are numbered XE1 to XE9, with Textile as XE9. Candidates answer XE0 plus at most two of XE1 to XE9. See the brochure's paper table for the full old-to-new mapping.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"XHPaper codeXH section codes renamedXH-B1 (Reasoning and Comprehension, common) is now XH0; XH-C1 to XH-C6 are now XH1 to XH6.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"XLPaper codeXL section codes renamedXL-P (Chemistry, common) is now XL0; XL-Q to XL-U are now XL1 to XL5.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"BTSyllabusBT: syllabus organized into 6 sectionsThe GATE 2027 BT syllabus has 6 sections, with bioreaction and bioprocess topics under Section 4, Fundamentals of Biological Engineering. Compare with your previous BT syllabus for topic-level differences.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026), Appendix D (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"ALLStructureTwo-paper combinations list updated (tentative)The allowed primary/secondary paper combinations include the new RA paper (for example CS, EC, EE, IN and ME can pair with RA). The list is marked tentative and subject to change.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026), Table 4 (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"ALLProcessRegistration: live facial capture and DigiLockerApplicants must provide live facial details during registration. A verified DigiLocker account is recommended; unverified accounts may be asked for additional documents.Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"ALLProcessExam datesGATE 2027 is scheduled for February 6, 7, 13, 14, 20 and 21, 2027 (forenoon and afternoon sessions).Source: GATE 2027 Information Brochure (IIT Madras, revised 27 Sep 2026) (opens in a new tab) · Verified on 2026-10-02\",\n  \"AE\",\n  \"AG\",\n  \"AR\",\n  \"BM\",\n  \"CE\",\n  \"CH\",\n  \"CS\",\n  \"CY\",\n  \"DA\",\n  \"EC\",\n  \"EE\",\n  \"ES\",\n  \"EY\",\n  \"GE\",\n  \"GG\",\n  \"IN\",\n  \"MA\",\n  \"ME\",\n  \"MN\",\n  \"MT\",\n  \"NM\",\n  \"PE\",\n  \"PH\",\n  \"PI\",\n  \"ST\"\n ],\n \"extLinks\": [\n  \"https://gate2027ib.iitm.ac.in/GATE2027-IB.pdf\",\n  \"https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/\"\n ]\n}"